/-! # The certificate value of a seven-vertex column

For each admissible labeled seven-vertex extension the certificate forms
a single integer over the common denominator `5040 * scale ^ 2`:

* the *deck*, the sum of the class numbers of the seven six-vertex graphs
  obtained by deleting one vertex;
* the one-root form, sampled over the seven rootings and the twenty ways
  of splitting the remaining six vertices into two triples;
* the root-triple form, sampled over the 210 ordered root triples and the
  six ways of splitting the remaining four vertices into two pairs, using
  the nonedge or the edge Gram matrix according to the root triple.

The certificate's claim is that this value never exceeds a fixed bound.

Everything is arranged so that a column costs only bit extraction and
array lookups. Each sampled subgraph is described by a *gather*: the
positions in the seven-vertex mask of the ten (or four, or twenty) source
bits, packed six bits per position, so the induced mask is read off
directly instead of recomputed from triple ranks. Canonical flag indices
and the Gram matrices are likewise tabulated once. -/

namespace FlagAlgebras.Core.Tetrahedron.FullSevenLong

open FlagAlgebras.Core

-- The tables below are large literals; elaborating and compiling tens of
-- thousands of numerals costs more than the default budgets allow.
set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option maxRecDepth 200000

/-- Read bits `0 .. i - 1` of the gather `g` into `acc`. Written as a
tail recursion rather than a fold over a range, so that a column costs no
allocation at all. -/
def gatherAux (g m : ℕ) : ℕ → ℕ → ℕ
  | 0, acc => acc
  | i + 1, acc =>
      gatherAux g m i
        (if m.testBit ((g >>> (6 * i)) &&& 63) then acc ||| (1 <<< i) else acc)

/-- Read `cnt` bits of `m` from the positions packed in `g`, six bits per
position, into a mask. -/
def gatherBits (g cnt m : ℕ) : ℕ := gatherAux g m cnt 0

